  "title": "Drug Resistant Candida auris Fungus Reported in 27 US States: What You Need to Know in 2026",
  "summary": "A drug resistant fungus known as Candida auris continues to spread across healthcare facilities in the United States, with the latest data from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) showing confirmed cases in 27 states during 2026. While the pace of new infections has slowed compared to previous years, health experts warn that the fungus remains a serious public health concern because of its resistance to common antifungal medications and its ability to spread rapidly in hospitals",
